*  earn0_disc_arbno_star_fence_positive.sno - DISCRIMINATING SIBLING for the
*  ARBNO(*cmd)-FENCE family (2026-08-12 s29).
*
*  WHY THIS EXISTS. crosscheck/patterns 119 / 129 / 148 / 149 all use this exact
*  cmd/outer idiom and all assert on the FAILURE branch (:S(BAD)F(GOOD)) -- their
*  expected outcome is that the match FAILS. A test that asserts FAILURE is passed by
*  ANY defect that causes failure, including total loss of the pattern: a degenerate
*  ARBNO(null) cannot span a multi-character subject between POS(0) and RPOS(0), so it
*  fails too, and prints the very same 'GOOD' string. Honest FENCE sealing and total
*  pattern loss are INDISTINGUISHABLE there.
*
*  THIS witness inverts the polarity: subject 'aa' makes the CORRECT answer a MATCH.
*    honest  : ARBNO(FENCE('a'|'ab')) takes 'a' then 'a' -> cursor 2 -> RPOS(0) -> MATCH
*    degenerate: ARBNO(null) matches only the empty string -> POS(0)..RPOS(0) on 'aa' -> FAIL
*  The separation is PROVEN by the poisoned control beside this file, which flips the
*  oracle's answer -- a discriminator whose arms give the same oracle answer is not one.
*
*  AT HEAD fc5b0754: SPITBOL MATCHES, SCRIP FAILS. Deterministic, rc=0, wrong answer.
*  ⇒ SCRIP cannot span 'aa' with this idiom, so 119/129/148/149 pass for a reason
*  unrelated to the seal they claim to test.
*  ⛔ DO NOT "fix" this by changing the subject back to one that fails. That is the
*  vacuity this witness exists to prevent.
        cmd   = FENCE('a' | 'ab')
        outer = ARBNO(*cmd)
        s     = 'aa'
        s POS(0) *outer RPOS(0)                               :S(GOOD)F(BAD)
GOOD    OUTPUT = 'arbno-star-cmd spanned aa'                  :(END)
BAD     OUTPUT = 'FAILED: pattern did not span aa'
END
